# Architecture and Boundaries

## Backend ownership
Backend owns:
- business rules
- authentication and authorization
- ownership checks
- pricing
- inventory reservation
- checkout validation
- payment verification
- order state transitions
- return/refund rules
- notification event processing
- audit events

## Database ownership
Database agent owns:
- Prisma schema
- migrations
- indexes
- constraints
- seed/test data
- query performance at schema level

Do not place business rules exclusively in the database.

## Customer ownership
Customer agent owns:
- customer-facing React Native screens
- navigation
- client state
- secure token storage abstraction
- platform adapters
- customer UI states

Customer must consume server-authoritative values.

## Admin ownership
Admin agent owns:
- admin React screens
- protected routes
- permission-aware navigation
- operational tables/forms/modals
- role-aware visibility

Admin must never rely only on UI hiding for authorization.

## Integration ownership
Integration agent owns:
- API client integration
- DTO/model mapping
- cross-platform contract alignment
- end-to-end wiring

## Shared files
Shared contracts, generated API types, configuration and common utilities are conflict-sensitive.
Only one agent may own a shared file at a time.
